<title>UK: S&amp;P rates Hitachi's $200 mln eurobond.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P rates Hitachi's $200 mln eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rating agency Standard and Poor's said on Monday it had assigned its AA long-term rating to Hitachi Credit Corp's $200 million Eurobonds due July 2002.</p>
<p>&quot;The rating reflects Hitachi Credit's stable earnings, adequate capital base and strong liquidity,&quot; S&amp;P said in a statement.  </p>
<p>It said an additional positive rating factor was the firm's relationship with its AAA rated parent Hitachi Ltd, which owns 52 percent of Hitachi Credit.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said the outlook was stable. &quot;Hitachi Credit's solid operating base, as well as its strong financial profile, should continue to mitigate the negative impact from the intensifying competitive environment,&quot; S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>-- International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 8682</p>
